mpensation: $6.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 78K people. Revenue per employee of $488K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $48K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["GE Vernova Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $185.1B market cap on $38.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 19% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $3.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.02\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 26\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 270% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitud